  "data": {
    "storage_and_data_notes": "Homepage mainly stores configuration files, service definitions, bookmarks, widget settings, and any secrets you choose to provide through files or environment variables. It does not need a database for the normal Docker setup.",
    "backup_details": "Back up the mounted config directory and any environment or secret files used by the container. A restore should prove that the same config folder can be mounted into a fresh container and that service widgets still load with the expected credentials.\n\nIf you use Docker labels for service discovery, remember that part of the dashboard state lives in your container labels, not only in the Homepage config folder. Keep your Compose files or deployment manifests backed up with the dashboard config.",
    "backup_difficulty": "very_easy",
    "backup_criticality": "medium",
    "raid_notes": "RAID is usually not important for Homepage itself. The useful protection is a versioned copy of the config folder and deployment files. RAID can help the server stay online, but it is not a backup."
  },
